  {
   "id": "F_b0qeacAAAJ",
   "from": "Jan Tünermann",
   "author": "7ab2d61d18fd7449",
   "date": "2016-01-27T23:05:21Z",
   "subject": "Avoiding Segmentation Faults in rstan 2.0.9 / R 3.2.2 / Ubuntu 15.10",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Dear all,\r<br>\r<br>I just installed rstan on a fresh Ubuntu 15.10 box and encountered \r<br>segmentation faults when running any models.\r<br>\r<br>When you encounter the same problem (as you would, I think, setting up \r<br>system with the current versions mentioned in the subject line, and \r<br>following the usual instructions):\r<br>\r<br>* Use remove.packages(&#39;rstan&#39;) to remove any already installed package\r<br>* remove.packages(&#39;Rcpp&#39;)\r<br>* Then, install.packages(&quot;Rcpp&quot;, type = &quot;source&quot;)\r<br>* And install.packages(&quot;rstan&quot;, type = &quot;source&quot;)\r<br>\r<br>(I saw this solution somewhere before for some older versions, probably \r<br>on this list).\r<br>\r<br>Best regards,\r<br>Jan\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
